# Coder Primitives Library

## Overview

This specification defines the shared Coder client library (Tier 2) that provides primitives for interacting with the Coder API. This library is used by:

1. **sudopod providers** - `CoderSelfHostedProvider` uses it directly
2. **sudocode-hub backend** - Uses it to manage workspaces on behalf of users

The library lives within the sudopod package at `src/providers/coder/client.ts`.

## Scope

This library handles:
- User management (create, get users)
- Workspace management (create, delete, get, start/stop workspaces)
- Template lookup (by name)
- Authentication handling (admin API token)

It does NOT handle:
- Template management (templates are pushed via coder CLI to coder-infra)
- Provider-level configuration (handled by Tier 1 providers)
- Deploy options parsing (handled by Tier 1 providers)
- Workspace listing (users can view their workspaces directly in Coder UI)

## API Design

### CoderClient Class

```typescript
// src/providers/coder/client.ts

export interface CoderClientConfig {
  /** Coder server URL (e.g., 'https://coder.company.com') */
  url: string;

  /** Admin API token for authentication */
  authToken: string;
}

export class CoderClient {
  constructor(config: CoderClientConfig);

  // Organization Management
  getOrganizations(): Promise<CoderOrganization[]>;
  getDefaultOrganizationId(): Promise<string>;

  // User Management
  ensureUserWithPassword(options: CreatePasswordUserOptions): Promise<CoderUser>;
  ensureUserWithOIDC(options: CreateOIDCUserOptions): Promise<CoderUser>;
  getUser(username: string): Promise<CoderUser>;
  deriveUsernameFromEmail(email: string): string;

  // Template Management
